---
/** How "Is it windy?" works, in plain words: a section of the About page on every site. */
import {
  MODELS,
  WIND,
  WIND_BANDS,
  WIND_BAND_LABELS,
  formatHour,
  toWindUnits,
  type WindBand,
} from '@isithot/core';

type Rising = Exclude<WindBand, 'calm'>;
/** "13 mph (21 km/h)": a band's edge in both units, as the sites show them. */
const both = (kmh: number): string => `${toWindUnits(kmh, 'mph')} mph (${kmh} km/h)`;
/** "Breezy from a wind of 13 mph (21 km/h) or gusts of 20 mph (32 km/h)." */
const bands = (WIND_BANDS.slice(1) as Rising[]).map(
  (band) =>
    `${WIND_BAND_LABELS[band]} from a wind of ${both(WIND.from[band].mean)} or gusts of ${both(WIND.from[band].gust)}.`,
);
const days = ['no', 'one', 'two', 'three', 'four', 'five', 'six', 'seven'];
const waking = `${formatHour(WIND.day.fromHour)} and ${formatHour(WIND.day.toHour)}`;
---

<h2>Is it windy?</h2>
<p>
  For wind, we ask {MODELS.length} forecast models for the wind and its gusts 10 metres above the
  ground, hour by hour, and take the middle of what they say (the median). A day is judged on its
  strongest wind and gusts between {waking}, the hours most people are out in it.
</p>
<p>
  The bands follow the Beaufort scale and the Met Office's own definitions of a gale and a storm,
  where the wind or its gusts can each be enough:
</p>
<ul>
  {bands.map((line) => (
    <li>{line}</li>
  ))}
</ul>
<p>
  Windy or more is Yes, and breezy is A bit. The strip under the answer shows each forecast's
  strongest gust, and the line above it how many forecasts put the day in the same band.
</p>
<p>
  Where the wind blows from is the forecasts' directions combined, each counting for as much as its
  wind is strong, at the windiest hour of the day. The arrows point where the wind is going, as the
  Met Office draws them, so a wind from the south-west (SW) points north-east. When the middle of
  the forecasts' winds is under {both(WIND.direction.fromMean)}, or the forecasts point different
  ways, no direction is given.
</p>
<p>
  Today means the rest of today, from the current hour to {formatHour(WIND.day.toHour)} (to midnight
  later in the evening), so a windy afternoon still to come counts. This week is Yes when{' '}
  {days[WIND.week.windyFrom]} or more days are windy or any day brings a gale, and Partly when fewer
  are windy.
  {WIND.normals.compare && (
    <>
      {' '}
      Where NASA POWER's long-term records cover it, we also compare the wind with what is normal
      there at this time of year, but only where the records' 50 km grid cell is within{' '}
      {WIND.normals.maxHeightDifference} m of the place's height: hills and coasts are much windier
      than the land around them.
    </>
  )}
</p>
<p>
  These sites do not issue warnings. For a gale or a storm at a place in the UK, the page links to
  the Met Office's official warnings.
</p>
